{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.CategoricalNeutronUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.CategoricalNeutronUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.unique_up_to_isotopy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.unique_up_to_isotopy","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L54-L71","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical neutron up to braid isotopy**\n(conditional on the Hecke-normal-form coincidence of\n[`def:categorical-neutron`]).\n\nTwo categorical neutrons with the same Hecke normal form in `H₃(q)` and the\nsame `S₃` colour assignment are equal.  This replaces the earlier\n`Subsingleton CategoricalNeutron` axiom, which was *false* for the free real\nfields `skein_ud, skein_dd`: distinct Skein data give genuinely distinct\nneutrons, so uniqueness holds only conditionally on a shared Hecke normal\nform — exactly the content of the narrative statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-neutron-unique","label":"prop:categorical-neutron-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.chirality","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Same chirality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.mass","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Same derived mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.skein_dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.skein_dd","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Same pair-Skein mass `S_dd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.skein_ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.skein_ud","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Same pair-Skein mass `S_ud`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NeutronSameHeckeNF","kind":"class","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L35-L52","doc":"**Hecke-normal-form coincidence context.**\n\nTwo categorical neutrons share the same Hecke normal form in `H₃(q)` and the\nsame `S₃` colour assignment.  By [`def:categorical-neutron`] the Hecke normal\nform determines the pair-Skein masses, the derived mass, and the chirality;\nthe `S₃` permutation symmetry on the colour tubes makes the assignment of\n`(u, d, d)` to tube positions irrelevant.  This class records that\ncoincidence as explicit hypotheses, so the uniqueness theorem below is a\nrigorous *conditional* result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.chirality","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Zero crossing chirality (electric charge `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.mass","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Mass `= 2·S_ud + S_dd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.skein_dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.skein_dd","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Pair Skein mass `S_dd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.skein_ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.skein_ud","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Pair Skein mass `S_ud`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalNeutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalNeutron","kind":"structure","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique.lean#L20-L33","doc":"Defining data of the categorical neutron (mirror of\n[`def:categorical-neutron`], `QOU.Torsion.CategoricalNeutron`): the\ncolour-linked triple `[u, d, d]_c ⋈ L_H` is determined by its pair-Skein\nmasses `(S_ud, S_dd)`, with derived mass `2·S_ud + S_dd` and zero crossing\nchirality. ","signatureChunk":0}]}